diff -ruN -x ORIGIN.md -x ORIGIN.sha256 -x ORIGIN.diff -x __pycache__ -x .DS_Store a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md	2026-11-01 00:29:12
+++ b/README.md	2026-11-01 12:44:38
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@
 
 Linked into XNU by `unixnu build kernel`.
 
+iPadOS 27 copy (xnu-12377): `ml_processor_register` boots the processor itself (`processor_boot`) and `processor_start` is a no-op, so this copy
+installs the interrupt path before it registers the boot CPU, runs `initCPU` once (`bootInitialized`), and sets a secondary's number and state
+before it registers it: from then on the new core owns its state. One processor set, no Edge, no `ml_cpu_init_completed`, as on iPadOS 17.
+
 Shared peripheral interrupts for drivers (C exports): `armcpu_spi_attach` (Group 1, priority 0xA0, routed to the boot CPU,
 enabled; the handler runs before the EOI and clears its level source), `armcpu_spi_count`, and `armcpu_spi_disable` /
 `armcpu_spi_enable` (GICD_ICENABLER with RWP / GICD_ISENABLER) for a line the caller attached; the slot stays, so a storm
